.TH AHERALD 1
.SH NAME
aherald \- desktop notifications for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aherald
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
aHerald delivers notifications for configured coding agents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --hook \fR[\fB--agent \fIclaude\fR|\fIcodex\fR]
Read one hook payload from standard input; Codex unless \fB--agent claude\fR is given.
.TP
.B --notify \fIHARNESS\fB --kind \fIKIND\fR [\fB--activity\fR|\fB--ended\fR]
Report an event of a harness without hooks (OpenCode, Pi, Goose, Crush).
\fIKIND\fR is turn_complete, permission_required, input_required, error or interrupted.
\fB--activity\fR reports that work resumed; \fB--ended\fR that the session ended (evidence only, never shown).
.TP
.B --demo \fR[\fISECONDS\fR]
Loop a configuration preview; exit through its tray menu.
.TP
.B --setup --harness \fINAME\fR
Configure the selected harnesses for this executable (a dry run unless \fB--apply\fR is given).
Use \fB--setup-executable \fIPATH\fR to bind the hooks to another executable.
.TP
.B --console-setup
Interactively select user hook integrations and usage settings.
.TP
.B --resident
Start the notification service for the current user.
.TP
.B --status
Show the current resident status.
.TP
.B --quit
Request a graceful resident shutdown.
.TP
.B --unsetup
Preview removal of this installation's saved user hook bindings.
Add \fB--apply\fR to perform the removal.
.TP
.B --help
List all options.
.SH FILES
The system package uses XDG user configuration, data and state directories.
See /usr/share/doc/aherald/installation.md for setup and removal details.
